{"id":"l1","level":6,"levelName":"Reading literature","n":1,"of":8,"title":"The vav that flips the tense","titleHe":"וָ״ו הַהִפּוּךְ","goal":"Read narrative past in biblical style — future forms that mean the past.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Biblical narrative doesn't tell a story in the past tense. It puts a וַ on the front of a future-tense verb, and the whole thing means the past. This is why a page of Genesis looks like it's about to happen and isn't."},{"type":"table","caption":"Reading it","head":["on the page","looks like","actually means"],"rows":[["וַיֹּאמֶר","he will say","and he said"],["וַיֵּלֶךְ","he will go","and he went"],["וַתֹּאמֶר","she will say","and she said"],["וַיְהִי","it will be","and it came to pass"],["וַיִּקְרָא","he will call","and he called"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"It works the other way too: וְ on a past-tense verb can push it into the future — וְהָיָה, and it shall be. Rarer, and mostly in prophecy."},{"type":"text","body":"You'll meet this in anything drawing on the Bible, which in Hebrew literature is nearly everything."}],"vocab":[{"he":"וַיֹּאמֶר","en":"and he said","translit":"vayomer"},{"he":"וַיְהִי","en":"and it came to pass","translit":"vayhi"},{"he":"וַיֵּלֶךְ","en":"and he went","translit":"vayelech"},{"he":"וַיַּרְא","en":"and he saw","translit":"vayar"},{"he":"וַתֹּאמֶר","en":"and she said","translit":"vatomer"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["answer","animal","one (m.)","and he said"],"correct":3,"prompt":"וַיֹּאמֶר","translit":"vayomer"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["good","and it came to pass","anger","short"],"correct":1,"prompt":"וַיְהִי","translit":"vayhi"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["dove","and he went","of","midrash, exposition"],"correct":1,"prompt":"וַיֵּלֶךְ","translit":"vayelech"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["tomato","feeling","approximately","and he saw"],"correct":3,"prompt":"וַיַּרְא","translit":"vayar"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["tasty","eleven (m.)","and she said","morning"],"correct":2,"prompt":"וַתֹּאמֶר","translit":"vatomer"},{"type":"choice","q":"Reading it — וַיֵּלֶךְ?","options":["and she said","and it came to pass","and he said","and he went"],"correct":3,"he":false},{"type":"read","he":"וַיֹּאמֶר","translit":"vayomer","en":"and he said"},{"type":"choice","q":"Reading it — וַיֹּאמֶר?","options":["and it came to pass","and she said","and he said","and he went"],"correct":2,"he":false},{"type":"choice","q":"Reading it — וַתֹּאמֶר?","options":["and he said","and it came to pass","and she said","and he went"],"correct":2,"he":false},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “and he saw”?","options":["מַדָּע","וַיַּרְא","אַגָּדָה","אֵם"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “and it came to pass”?","options":["וַיְהִי","אֶל","שָׁחֹר","שֵׁן"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Reading it — וַיְהִי?","options":["and it came to pass","and she said","and he went","and he said"],"correct":0,"he":false},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “and she said”?","options":["אֵיךְ","מַדָּע","בִּכְלָל","וַתֹּאמֶר"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["וַיְהִי","וַיֹּאמֶר","וַתֹּאמֶר","וַיֵּלֶךְ"],"correct":2,"say":"וַתֹּאמֶר","he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["וַיֹּאמֶר","and he said"],["וַיְהִי","and it came to pass"],["וַיֵּלֶךְ","and he went"],["וַיַּרְא","and he saw"],["וַתֹּאמֶר","and she said"]]},{"type":"type","q":"Write “and he saw” in Hebrew","answer":"וַיַּרְא","hint":"vayar"}]}